From 919445884f55cfe406df22e4e3d440692cc1b12a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mr-2c <158831365+Mr-2c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 11:54:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Flush log output during initialization, around file output,
 and on errors

Backport of upstream PR #2643 (squash-merge 760f0690d2f) onto the v1.1.1
release tag. The PR merged into `develop` about seven hours before v1.1.1
was published, but the release was not cut from that line, so v1.1.1 does
not contain it.

Adds deterministic, event-based flushing so the log survives a process
death (crash, OOM-kill, scheduler kill) instead of being discarded from
the Fortran runtime's I/O buffer:

* `log_t` gains a `flush()` type-bound procedure, guarded on rank 0 and
  never collective.
* Log level parameters move above the type so the components can carry
  default initializers; `log_free` now flushes and resets the unit to
  stdout.
* The banner, warnings and the C interface entry points flush after
  writing; `log_error` flushes the buffered log and then routes through
  `neko_error`.
* The four error routines in `utils.f90` flush `output_unit` before
  reporting and `error_unit` before `error stop`; `neko_warning` flushes
  after writing.
* The boundary-condition validation errors in `fluid_pnpn` and
  `scalar_pnpn` go through `neko_error` instead of writing to
  `error_unit` directly.
* `output_controller_execute` and the joblimit checkpoint flush around
  file writes.

Backport notes, relative to the upstream commit:

* `src/scalar/scalar_pnpn.f90` - upstream's context imports
  `BC_DIRICHLET` from `bc`, which does not exist on v1.1.1. The v1.1.1
  import is kept and only `use utils, only : neko_error` is added.
* `src/.depends` - `common/utils.lo` is added to the v1.1.1 form of the
  `scalar/scalar_pnpn.lo` line.

All other hunks apply unmodified; `log.f90` and `utils.f90` are
byte-identical to the upstream merged versions.

